{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558663-quintessence-economy","id":1558663,"title":"Quintessence Economy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-03-05T09:45:36-08:00","id":1558663,"title":"Quintessence Economy","content":"I got to thinking about how much quintessence characters will have access to. One of my complaints about some passages in M20 and associated books is high Quint costs, but that\u2019s based on intuition. So I figured I\u2019d list the ways a mage can get quintessence.<br /> <br /> Starting off with nodes. Nodes come in a range from 1 to 10 and how much quintessence they give varies with the tone of the game, but the default assumption for modern times is 2 points per week per level, half in free quintessence and half in tass. A 5 point node, then would generate 10 points per week, which is pretty good for a single mage and thin for an entire circle.<br /> <br /> Then there\u2019s the matter of getting it out and using it, which is highly dependent on Prime ranks.<br /> <hr /><br /> At 0 Prime:<br /> <br /> A mage with no dots in Prime can meditate at the node to absorb some of what is there. I can\u2019t find hard rules on the meditation, but I would imagine a period of time meditating lets him roll something like Perception + Meditation to determine how many points he can absorb. He is limited to holding, at most, his Avatar rating in quintessence and can use, at most, his Avatar rating in points in a single roll (or turn).<br /> <br /> There is also some indication that if he has Tass in a form he can consume (like, say, an energy drink) he can add that Quintessence to his pool by consuming it. He is still limited by is Avatar rating for both amount and rate.<br /> <br /> If none of a circle has Prime they are going to be very limited in how much quintessence they can absorb and use. If we presume a circle of 5 mages with Avatar 2, they can at most hold 10 quintessence points among them at any one time.<br /> <hr /><br /> At 1 Prime:<br /> <br /> Just being able to sense quintessence lets a mage store dramatically more than his Avatar rating, potentially up to 20 points.<br /> <br /> For group dynamics this means that any mage with Prime 1 can hold a lot more, but without higher levels they can\u2019t really share it. Of course without a good source, they can\u2019t really access much more than they already could. This rank doesn't expand what quintessence a mage has access to.<br /> <hr /><br /> At Prime 2:<br /> <br /> There is almost no change at this level except\u2026 if the mage happens to be fortunate enough to have a periapt he can pull quintessence out of it. It is unclear if he can put quintessence into it, but lets say yes for now.<br /> <br /> This, potentially, lets any mages in the group with Prime 2 share quintessence. Plus they can store more if we count the periapt.<br /> <hr /><br /> At Prime 3:<br /> <br /> This is where things take a dramatic step up. Firstly a mage with Prime 3 is no longer limited by his Avatar rating when moving or using quintessence. Also he can move quintessence around. He can magically pull it from nodes and junctures and any kind of tass without meditation, though he is still limited to what is available in them.<br /> He can also make periapts and move quintessence to his fellow mages, which is a huge boon for a circle. Only one mage has to have Prime 3 to dramatically increase the groups ability to transfer quintessence between them.<br /> <br /> Also, the sources of quintessence go up dramatically. At Prime 3, mages can pull quintessence out of living sacrifices, in ranges of 5 points for a small animal and going up from there. He can also sacrifice objects and possibly energies, though the amount this gives is unclear (likely equivalent to the structure of the object). He can pull quintessence from that freed by a large fire at a rate determined by the base damage and duration chart (approx. 2 per success). He can change the successes of a physical attack into points of quintessence pulled from the target, or drain an incoming attack turning every level he soaks into quintessence. All of these new sources will carry the resonance of the act, which might sometimes be a problem, but still, the amount of quintessence available goes up dramatically.<br /> <br /> It is worth noting that the resonance of sacrifice is not automatically dark. It could also carry resonances appropriate to various religions throughout history.<br /> <hr /><br /> At Prime 4:<br /> <br /> Another jump up in capabilities. Now mages can use Prime to pull the quintessence straight out of a matter or energy pattern instead of having to destroy the object and pull in what was released. The actual amounts are still unclear. The common magical effects chart also indicates a mage can pull more quintessence from a Node than it produces though this is damaging to the Node. I haven\u2019t found a system for this yet.<br /> <br /> Tap Wellspring is also available which means energetic events become a source of quintessence (and associated resonance). The rules are somewhere in HDYDT, but I don\u2019t have them written down.<br /> <br /> A mage with Prime 4 can also make Tass, which means he can make it in consumable forms, which is a useful way of getting it to teammates when he is not directly there. Overall a small boost up from Prime 3.<br /> <hr /><br /> Finally at Prime 5:<br /> <br /> A Prime Master can pull quintessence from anywhere, likely using the base damage and duration chart, which is a huge leap in accessibility. He can also use Prime to destroy a creature directly and absorb quintessence. Unlike with sacrifice this is likely always tainted with dark resonance.<br /> <br /> With great difficulty (I think it is 10 successes per level) he can create a node or increase one that already exists. This is likely not too much of a step up for the master himself but a dramatic boon for his circle.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, that\u2019s what I\u2019ve found so far, without even dipping into Primal Ventures. What I\u2019m seeing here is that there is a dramatic difference depending on if the group has access to Prime 3 or not. A Prime 3 mage could reasonably pull in dozens of points of quintessence in a week if he needed to. Any other sources you can think of?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T15:02:05-07:00","id":1561939,"title":"","content":"I think we need to consider the Economy in social terms, too.<br /> <br /> First, Tass can be directly consumed in Magic. Even with Avatar 0 and Prime 0, a Mage can use Tass as long as they integrate it into their Instruments. That makes Tass the actual basis of the Quintessence economy in the game.<br /> <br /> Prime 3+ let a Mage create sources for other Mages. This isn't just a boon to a cabal: it's a way to distribute further and a commodity to buy and sell.<br /> <br /> So you don't dial availability of Quintessence just by adjusting Node production, you do so even more by deciding how easy it is to procure Tass among the Awakened society, and Prime Mages increase this availability just by existing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T15:06:01-07:00","id":1561941,"title":"","content":"I'd need to track down the exact page number, but I'm fairly sure there's an offhand remark in HDYDT indicating all Mages can absorb the Quint from Tass in the same manner as meditating at a Node.<br /> <br /> Found it after I made my own post about the same topic a while ago <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T15:23:33-07:00","id":1561944,"title":"","content":"That would be a direct contradiction of the actual rules in the core. Which isn't weird for HDYDT, but I'll pass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}